# Mobile Demo Boundary

`src/mobile/` is a separate demo surface with its own Vite entry (`/mobile.html`). It must stay decoupled from the desktop demo so the two can evolve independently.

Mobile code may import ONLY from the shared design-system layer:

- `@/components/ui`, `@/icons`, `@/styles`, `@/index.css`, `@/assets`
- `@/lib` and `@/config` only for pieces that are genuinely surface-agnostic

Mobile code must NOT import desktop-only code:

- `@/components/{desktop,window,layout,tile,tabs,chat,sidebar,content}`
- `@/store`, `@/data`, `@/types`, `@/App`

Other rules:

- Mobile owns its state: stores, types, and seed data live under `src/mobile/`. Never reuse desktop zustand stores.
- Nothing outside `src/mobile/` may import from `src/mobile/`.
- If a shared-layer piece turns out to be desktop-flavored, fork it into `src/mobile/` instead of adding mobile branches to the shared code.
